# JusPrin 2 launch email, batch 1: why opens are low (working notes, 2026-11-13)

No personal data in this file. Recipient lists stay in the parent session's scratchpad/wave/ (chmod 600).

## Open curve (SendGrid Marketing Campaigns LEGACY, campaign 22621835, sent 6:51 AM PST Nov 13)
- 9:35 AM PST: 301 delivered, 21 unique opens (6.98%), 31 total opens, 1 unique click (GitHub download link).
- Openers: 18 gmail.com/googlemail.com (18/241 = 7.5% of Gmail recipients), 2 ufcat.edu.br, 1 custom domain.
  0 of 26 hotmail.com, 6 outlook.*, 6 yahoo.com.br, 3 icloud.com opened.

## Earlier campaigns, same SendGrid account and unsubscribe group
| Campaign | Sender | End of day 1 | Final |
| JusPrin public release b1 (May 2025) | Obi The Owl <support@obico.io> | 30.5% | 47.8% |
| JusPrin 1.1.0 to non-English users (Jun 2025, English subject) | same | 37.5% | 65.4% |
| JusPrin 1.3.0 (Aug 2025, sent 3:48 PM) | same | 11.1% | 33.2% |
| JusPrin 1.4.0 (Oct 2025, 4,124 JusPrin users) | same | 26.1% | 41.6% |
| Re-Inventing TSD b1 (Feb 2026) | same | 16.6% | 55.7% |
| Next-Gen AI b2 (Apr 2026) | same | 33.8% | 43.8% |
(SendGrid's day boundary is not documented; "end of day 1" is the first CSV row.)
- Gmail-only unique open rate (mailbox provider stats): Oct 19-25 2025 = 47%; Feb 2026 = 46%; Apr 2026 = 42%.
  So the drop is inside Gmail, not a change in Apple Mail share.

## Who opened: flat across every kind of recipient
Production (read-only) for the 310: 157 signed up in the last 30 days, 55 over a year ago; 204 signed up with Google.
Opens: signed up <=30d 11/157 = 7%, 31-365d 6/98 = 6%, >1y 4/55 = 7%; chatted on 1 day 5/103, 4+ days 11/136.
=> not explained by new or throwaway accounts (3 disposable-mail domains exist, but heavy and old users open at the same rate).

## Sender
- Batch 1: "Kenneth from JusPrin" <jusprin-support@obico.io>; SendGrid sender created ~Nov 12 (JusPrin Support variant ~Nov 8).
- Every earlier campaign: "Obi The Owl" <support@obico.io>, in use since 2022.

## Headers and bounces
- Legacy campaign test copy (Message 1a1d552727576b3f in k@obico.io, now in Trash) carries List-Unsubscribe + List-Unsubscribe-Post: One-Click. SPF/DKIM pass. So THIS email meets one-click; Postmaster's "needs work" is domain-wide (Obico server mail, PR 1176).

